2. Inheritance and Polymorphism: To demonstrate inheritance and runtime polymorphism. 

a) Create a base class Person and derived class Employee. 

Aim:
To create a base class Person and a derived class Employee using inheritance in Java.

PROGRAM :- 

// Base class
class Person {
    String name = "Rahul";
    int age = 30;

    void displayPerson() {
        System.out.println("Name: " + name);
        System.out.println("Age: " + age);
    }
}

// Derived class
class Employee extends Person {
    int empId = 101;

    void displayEmployee() {
        System.out.println("Employee ID: " + empId);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Employee e = new Employee();

        e.displayPerson();    // Inherited method
        e.displayEmployee();  // Employee method
    }
}

OUTPUT :- 

Name: Rahul
Age: 30
Employee ID: 101

B.Demonstrate Single Inheritance

Aim:
To demonstrate single inheritance in Java.

Program :- 

// Parent class
class Person {
    String name = "Rahul";

    void showName() {
        System.out.println("Name: " + name);
    }
}

// Child class
class Employee extends Person {
    int empId = 101;

    void showEmployee() {
        System.out.println("Employee ID: " + empId);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Employee e = new Employee();

        // Accessing parent class method
        e.showName();

        // Accessing child class method
        e.showEmployee();
    }
}

OUTPUT :- 

Name: Rahul
Employee ID: 101

C.Override a Method to Show Runtime Polymorphism

Aim
To demonstrate runtime polymorphism using method overriding in Java.

Program :-

// Parent class
class Person {
    void display() {
        System.out.println("This is Person class.");
    }
}

// Child class
class Employee extends Person {
    @Override
    void display() {
        System.out.println("This is Employee class.");
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Parent class reference, Child class object
        Person p = new Employee();

        // Runtime Polymorphism
        p.display();
    }
}


OUTPUT :- 

This is Employee class.

d): Use super Keyword

Aim
To demonstrate the use of the super keyword in Java.

Program :- 

// Parent class
class Person {
    String name = "Rahul";
}

// Child class
class Employee extends Person {
    String name = "Priya";

    void display() {
        System.out.println("Child Name : " + name);
        System.out.println("Parent Name: " + super.name);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Employee e = new Employee();
        e.display();
    }
}

OUTPUT :- 

Child Name : Priya
Parent Name: Rahul

